WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.812 --> 00:00:37.073
Endless landscapes,

00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:40.115
crossed by Indians dressed in their ponchos,

00:00:40.756 --> 00:00:42.196
this postcard image,

00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:43.457
This is Bolivia.

00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:44.698
This country,

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:46.800
the poorest in Latin America,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.961
As large as twice the size of France,

00:00:49.321 --> 00:00:50.902
is populated by 9 million inhabitants.

00:00:51.963 --> 00:00:54.345
More than 2 million of them live in La Paz,

00:00:54.506 --> 00:00:55.266
the capital,

00:00:55.546 --> 00:00:57.007
and its suburb El Alto,

00:00:57.487 --> 00:01:00.129
the great popular city of Indians and sailors.

00:01:01.369 --> 00:01:04.652
These two cities lie at the foot of the sacred mountains of the Altiplano,

00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:11.734
a vast and high plateau that stretches along the Royal Cordillera of the Andes and extends into its neighbors in Chile,

00:01:12.314 --> 00:01:13.914
from Argentina and Peru.

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:21.696
My name is Gerarda Morales.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:23.917
I am Indian and Mara.

00:01:24.397 --> 00:01:25.817
like a quarter of my Bolivian brothers.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:30.359
I am descended from a civilization that is over 3000 years old.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.780
of the first great Andean empire,

00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:34.481
that of Tihuanacu,

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.742
founded on the shores of Lake Titicaca.

00:01:39.543 --> 00:01:42.304
Our ancestors had extensive knowledge of agronomy.

00:01:42.544 --> 00:01:43.445
in architecture,

00:01:43.786 --> 00:01:45.125
in medicine and astronomy.

00:01:46.926 --> 00:01:48.087
We are a proud people.

00:01:49.332 --> 00:01:50.393
We love our languages.

00:01:50.673 --> 00:01:51.454
our traditions,

00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:52.895
our gods,

00:01:53.695 --> 00:01:56.498
our way of life on these otherwise hostile high plateaus.

00:02:01.782 --> 00:02:02.582
I live in the city,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:03.644
in El Alto.

00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:05.746
Here,

00:02:05.746 --> 00:02:07.766
We are almost at an altitude of 4000 meters.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.932
I see these majestic mountains every day.

00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:17.975
The very highest peaks are covered with glaciers.

00:02:19.743 --> 00:02:20.304
Ilimani,

00:02:20.805 --> 00:02:21.385
the Iliampu,

00:02:22.126 --> 00:02:23.105
the Wainapotosi,

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:24.546
the Tchakaltaya.

00:02:25.867 --> 00:02:26.367
In our country,

00:02:26.849 --> 00:02:28.990
These are gods worshipped throughout the country.

00:02:32.453 --> 00:02:34.493
Bolivia is experiencing a paradox.

00:02:34.794 --> 00:02:36.435
With global warming,

00:02:36.474 --> 00:02:37.735
Glaciers provide a lot of water.

00:02:38.235 --> 00:02:41.718
But the melting accelerated so much that it could not be anticipated.

00:02:42.098 --> 00:02:44.219
So this excess water is lost.

00:02:46.322 --> 00:02:47.021
In the Altiplano,

00:02:47.343 --> 00:02:49.343
We do not benefit from the water from glaciers.

00:02:49.543 --> 00:02:50.405
intended for the city.

00:02:50.844 --> 00:02:59.070
Climate change is resulting in a continuous decrease in rainfall, leading to a growing rural exodus towards El Alto.

00:03:04.394 --> 00:03:08.377
This demographic shift exacerbates the city's water access problems.

00:03:08.679 --> 00:03:11.620
primarily due to poverty and the outdated state of the network.

00:03:32.216 --> 00:03:32.736
In El Alto,

00:03:32.816 --> 00:03:33.736
I have a small house,

00:03:34.097 --> 00:03:35.057
almost at the edge of town,

00:03:36.057 --> 00:03:37.019
in the Inti neighborhood,

00:03:37.718 --> 00:03:39.599
which means the sunny district.

00:03:41.562 --> 00:03:43.403
I run a small recycling business there.

00:03:44.462 --> 00:03:46.123
That's partly how I earn a living.

00:03:47.465 --> 00:03:48.826
I collect plastics,

00:03:49.026 --> 00:03:49.526
metals,

00:03:50.407 --> 00:03:51.507
everything that can be recycled,

00:03:52.427 --> 00:03:54.629
and I resell them to a processing company.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.371
This reduces waste and there is less of it along the roads.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.721
I also teach from time to time.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.402
I learned traditional crafts from my mother and then I continued to make them myself.

00:04:08.403 --> 00:04:10.003
All of this provides a living for my father and me.

00:04:12.604 --> 00:04:15.706
I am also the president of a producers' association,

00:04:15.766 --> 00:04:18.228
farmers and artisans of the Altiplano.

00:04:19.043 --> 00:04:19.543
ICAB,

00:04:20.444 --> 00:04:23.968
which means integration of the emara communities of Bolivia.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:32.355
I regularly travel the roads of the Altiplano to meet my brothers and sisters from the association.

00:04:33.427 --> 00:04:37.248
More than 50 families spread across 24 rural communities.

00:04:45.091 --> 00:04:46.731
I haven't always lived in El Alto.

00:04:47.872 --> 00:04:49.612
I arrived here 25 years ago.

00:04:50.593 --> 00:04:51.093
Before,

00:04:51.113 --> 00:04:53.175
I used to live in a small village not far from here,

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.375
at Colque Alta,

00:04:54.675 --> 00:04:55.414
with my family.

00:04:56.675 --> 00:04:57.515
I was a shepherdess.

00:04:58.757 --> 00:05:02.779
And it was my brother, a schoolteacher, who wanted me to go and study in the city to ensure a better life for myself.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.701
That's what happened to me.

00:05:05.401 --> 00:05:07.204
but this is not the case for all migrants in El Alto.

00:05:13.969 --> 00:05:15.690
When I arrived in this new neighborhood,

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.031
There was no running water.

00:05:18.112 --> 00:05:20.175
I had to go get the water from Valentina's,

00:05:20.235 --> 00:05:20.814
my neighbor,

00:05:20.954 --> 00:05:22.235
which had a private well.

00:05:34.538 --> 00:05:34.858
NOW,

00:05:34.858 --> 00:05:36.899
I have a tap in my home and it has changed my life.

00:05:37.899 --> 00:05:39.661
But not everyone is in the same boat.

00:05:40.341 --> 00:05:42.402
Some neighborhoods do not have running water.

00:05:50.426 --> 00:05:52.548
El Alto is a long, narrow city.

00:05:52.827 --> 00:05:54.548
It stretches for several kilometers.

00:05:54.909 --> 00:05:55.969
Less than a century ago,

00:05:56.349 --> 00:05:57.971
It was just a suburb of La Paz,

00:05:58.151 --> 00:05:58.891
the capital.

00:05:59.399 --> 00:05:59.899
Today,

00:06:00.401 --> 00:06:01.343
this popular city,

00:06:01.362 --> 00:06:02.463
predominantly Emara

00:06:02.923 --> 00:06:05.247
it alone has almost a million inhabitants.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:06.307
Each day,

00:06:06.709 --> 00:06:09.512
New migrants from the Altiplano are settling there.

00:06:09.913 --> 00:06:13.016
The city's population growth reaches 5%

00:06:13.437 --> 00:06:13.937
per year.

00:06:15.278 --> 00:06:17.000
Water is a problem in El Alto.

00:06:17.562 --> 00:06:19.063
This one comes from glaciers.

00:06:19.436 --> 00:06:22.599
And it is difficult for the poorest populations to access.

00:06:28.864 --> 00:06:35.649
Most residents cannot afford the $150 for individual connection and consumption charges.

00:06:36.009 --> 00:06:38.932
knowing that the average salary is $100.

00:06:39.412 --> 00:06:43.916
Neighborhoods without mains water connections have communal fountains or wells.

00:06:47.992 --> 00:06:52.397
The town hall connected us to drinking water because the whole neighborhood mobilized for months.

00:06:53.758 --> 00:06:56.280
I know that the water we use comes from glaciers,

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:59.223
that global warming is responsible for their melting.

00:06:59.904 --> 00:07:00.665
And I'm worried about it.

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:03.948
As president of ICAB,

00:07:04.309 --> 00:07:06.130
I requested an interview with the mayor.

00:07:07.011 --> 00:07:11.496
We would like to know about his program for private access to drinking water for the residents of Alalto.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:25.791
Mr. Mayor,

00:07:25.851 --> 00:07:30.955
I would like to ask you a few questions about the number of inhabitants and the distribution of water according to the districts.

00:07:34.278 --> 00:07:37.040
El Alto has approximately one million inhabitants.

00:07:39.782 --> 00:07:40.483
Currently,

00:07:40.503 --> 00:07:44.486
Water reserves are insufficient for the entire population.

00:07:46.448 --> 00:07:51.132
This means almost 250,000 people are not supplied with drinking water.

00:07:52.216 --> 00:07:55.198
Because its distribution is not yet guaranteed for everyone.

00:07:56.798 --> 00:08:02.821
The unplanned population growth of our city is the cause of this poor water management.

00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:06.182
A significant number of migrants are arriving,

00:08:06.422 --> 00:08:07.083
settle in,

00:08:07.843 --> 00:08:08.943
build their habitat.

00:08:09.984 --> 00:08:11.324
Their primary need is water.

00:08:12.765 --> 00:08:13.605
What I mean is,

00:08:15.586 --> 00:08:18.327
It's not that we're refusing to supply these people with water,

00:08:18.527 --> 00:08:20.088
these 250,000 people.

00:08:21.989 --> 00:08:27.552
But the problem is that we have not yet succeeded in connecting them to the main water distribution networks.

00:08:29.753 --> 00:08:34.896
Often,
new housing developments do not have water for the first two months after they are built.

00:08:37.137 --> 00:08:42.660
One of our major concerns is that they have one or two public fountains available in the meantime.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:49.204
And one of the first concerns is the extension of a gallery so that there is at least...

00:08:49.624 --> 00:08:51.485
one or two common pilettes.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:34.394
Go ahead,

00:09:34.494 --> 00:09:36.797
You're going to leave.

00:09:55.119 --> 00:09:55.779
Mr. Mayor,

00:09:56.419 --> 00:09:59.140
We visited the Santa Cruz maritime district.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:07.442
And we found that people were using wells or the few public fountains because they didn't have access to water at home.

00:10:08.723 --> 00:10:11.984
A large number of them have applied to the town hall for water.

00:10:12.204 --> 00:10:13.324
but nothing came of it.

00:10:13.844 --> 00:10:15.365
They had to fend for themselves.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:23.971
This place is important for the community.

00:10:25.092 --> 00:10:27.974
This is the only public water source in this area.

00:10:29.635 --> 00:10:31.876
We would like to have a water supply in every house.

00:10:32.797 --> 00:10:35.219
But there are so many steps to take and it's so expensive.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:37.500
And as you know,

00:10:37.501 --> 00:10:38.861
The government doesn't have the resources.

00:10:39.041 --> 00:10:41.183
We are responsible for covering all installation costs.

00:10:49.523 --> 00:10:52.604
Where does the water come from?

00:10:53.985 --> 00:10:56.226
We brought it from the Santo Domingo neighborhood.

00:10:57.726 --> 00:10:58.907
And in order to achieve this,

00:10:58.947 --> 00:10:59.947
Everyone had to participate.

00:11:01.728 --> 00:11:02.308
All the neighbors?

00:11:04.309 --> 00:11:04.809
Of course,

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.191
We all worked the land with our own tools.

00:11:11.515 --> 00:11:13.841
Everyone also provided financial support.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.436
Each neighbor was assigned a work site of approximately 4 tons.

00:11:19.436 --> 00:11:20.797
We dug a trench 4 meters wide,

00:11:21.597 --> 00:11:23.418
Then we took care of the piping,

00:11:24.378 --> 00:11:26.859
and finally we had to buy more accessories.

00:11:30.721 --> 00:11:33.662
The box that protects the tap was made by us.

00:11:36.363 --> 00:11:41.205
All participants were given a key to open the padlock.

00:11:42.846 --> 00:11:43.526
Of course,

00:11:43.606 --> 00:11:46.888
Those who did not provide financial assistance are not entitled to the key.

00:11:50.725 --> 00:11:51.425
Mr. Mayor,

00:11:52.486 --> 00:11:54.527
if we don't address the melting of the glaciers,

00:11:54.927 --> 00:11:56.528
We will run out of water more and more.

00:11:56.788 --> 00:11:57.488
year after year.

00:11:58.168 --> 00:11:59.509
What solution is being offered to him?

00:12:08.753 --> 00:12:13.615
I am not an expert when it comes to water and its distribution in El Alto.

00:12:15.356 --> 00:12:18.557
But specialists will be able to find solutions to these future problems.

00:12:23.918 --> 00:12:24.639
What I know,

00:12:25.439 --> 00:12:27.359
The problem is getting worse.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:35.742
Technicians are predicting a very significant decrease in water due to the melting of our glaciers within the next 5 years.

00:12:36.742 --> 00:12:40.523
As it currently constitutes the most important source of water supply,

00:12:41.523 --> 00:12:42.804
This is therefore very worrying.

00:12:43.584 --> 00:12:44.124
Moreover,

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:48.143
We also have technical problems with the drinking water network.

00:12:49.364 --> 00:12:50.525
In anticipation of all this,

00:12:50.726 --> 00:12:55.610
Citizens must learn to be careful and to conserve this vital resource.

00:12:56.571 --> 00:13:00.314
And we must let the specialists do their work so that they can find the right solutions.

00:13:02.016 --> 00:13:06.400
The waste of tap water has reached considerable proportions in El Alto.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.001
up to 40%

00:13:08.061 --> 00:13:08.822
of water loss.

00:13:09.402 --> 00:13:11.084
Water seeping into the ground,

00:13:11.544 --> 00:13:14.525
The network is leaking due to the age of the pipes,

00:13:15.065 --> 00:13:18.266
not to mention the population that connects illegally.

00:13:18.986 --> 00:13:20.407
The solutions are obvious.

00:13:20.827 --> 00:13:27.629
To restore the water distribution network to working order and to build dams in the mountains to regulate the water from the glaciers.

00:13:28.149 --> 00:13:28.649
Simple,

00:13:29.109 --> 00:13:33.510
but exorbitant for a city that lives below the poverty line.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.191
And it's urgent.

00:13:35.751 --> 00:13:36.831
because in 2050,

00:13:37.171 --> 00:13:39.412
The region's population will have doubled.

00:13:49.036 --> 00:13:51.557
The Jackal Taïa is living its last ice age.

00:13:51.697 --> 00:13:53.117
Just a few years ago,

00:13:53.337 --> 00:13:56.738
This small glacier was the highest ski area in the world.

00:13:57.478 --> 00:14:09.882
The average annual rainfall deficit in the Chacal Taïa area increased from 60 cm of water between 1963 and 1983 to more than 1.20 m between 1983 and 2003.

00:14:10.242 --> 00:14:12.663
thus accelerating the melting of the glacier.

00:14:13.443 --> 00:14:14.303
80%

00:14:14.323 --> 00:14:17.764
Glaciers in the Andes are similar in size to the Taia jackal.

00:14:18.328 --> 00:14:20.829
and will have disappeared before the end of the century.

00:14:26.211 --> 00:14:28.792
The mountain gods in our region are called the achachilas.

00:14:30.173 --> 00:14:40.978
Honoring the deities is important in our traditions.

00:14:48.637 --> 00:14:49.557
I asked José,

00:14:49.837 --> 00:14:51.558
a Yatiri sorcerer whom I know well,

00:14:52.299 --> 00:14:56.381
to come and make offerings on the Chacaltaya to protect its last snows.

00:14:58.382 --> 00:14:58.962
In Aymara,

00:14:59.403 --> 00:15:01.023
Chacaltaya means icy road.

00:15:02.024 --> 00:15:03.285
I,
I saw him disappear.

00:15:05.446 --> 00:15:07.407
We live in harmony with the land and sea.

00:15:07.647 --> 00:15:08.408
Pachamama.

00:15:09.308 --> 00:15:11.269
Goddess among goddesses,

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.430
which brings abundance to those who worship it.

00:15:15.551 --> 00:15:19.674
Our ancestors always respected the divine signs observed in the sky and in nature.

00:15:20.214 --> 00:15:21.335
to know when to sow,

00:15:21.635 --> 00:15:22.355
when to harvest.

00:15:25.617 --> 00:15:28.118
José invokes Pachamama and the Achachilas.

00:15:28.218 --> 00:15:28.979
the mountain gods.

00:15:30.419 --> 00:15:31.760
He asks them for mercy.

00:15:33.161 --> 00:15:34.402
He wants to calm their anger.

00:15:44.178 --> 00:15:45.298
The fire must burn well.

00:15:45.839 --> 00:15:47.139
Otherwise, it's a bad omen.

00:15:47.919 --> 00:15:50.100
The sign that we have not prayed sincerely.

00:16:55.206 --> 00:16:57.706
Located less than 100 km from El Alto,

00:16:58.086 --> 00:17:02.848
The glaciers of the Cordillera Real provide most of the region's water consumption.

00:17:03.528 --> 00:17:06.869
The melting of glaciers has accelerated over the last ten years.

00:17:07.269 --> 00:17:08.389
In 1980,

00:17:08.729 --> 00:17:11.170
Scientists have calculated that Huayna Potosi,

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.351
a glacier in the Zongo Valley,

00:17:13.811 --> 00:17:16.512
had receded by 30 meters in 200 years.

00:17:16.992 --> 00:17:17.812
Since that date,

00:17:18.168 --> 00:17:19.129
In less than 30 years,

00:17:19.569 --> 00:17:20.430
He lost again

00:17:21.011 --> 00:17:21.731
50 meters.

00:17:22.092 --> 00:17:25.154
This is the conclusion reached by glaciologists from the IRD.

00:17:25.255 --> 00:17:27.597
the Research Institute for Development,

00:17:27.917 --> 00:17:32.401
which monitors the evolution of glaciers in the Andes, and particularly those in Bolivia.

00:17:34.743 --> 00:17:36.725
If we invoke the gods with enough faith,

00:17:37.846 --> 00:17:39.408
Then our wishes can come true.

00:17:40.749 --> 00:17:43.391
But I want to understand the misfortune that is striking our mountains.

00:17:44.212 --> 00:17:48.396
and to know everything that is within the power of men to fight against the agony of our glaciers.

00:17:50.258 --> 00:17:52.140
I wanted to accompany Edson and Patrick,

00:17:52.521 --> 00:17:53.341
two glaciologists,

00:17:53.582 --> 00:17:54.663
up to the Zongo glacier.

00:18:05.673 --> 00:18:08.093
Is this your first time going up onto a glacier?

00:18:08.693 --> 00:18:09.153
Yes,

00:18:09.153 --> 00:18:09.934
This is the first time.

00:18:10.634 --> 00:18:11.134
You'll see,

00:18:11.434 --> 00:18:12.414
You won't regret it.

00:18:13.215 --> 00:18:13.915
It's magnificent.

00:18:14.635 --> 00:18:15.135
Yes,

00:18:15.715 --> 00:18:21.517
I am always dazzled by the spectacle and what's more, the weather is beautiful today.

00:18:21.677 --> 00:18:24.878
Let's enjoy this splendor and sit down for a moment if you don't mind.

00:18:41.146 --> 00:18:43.408
We are still at 5500 meters,

00:18:43.848 --> 00:18:45.209
very close to the Zongo glacier,

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.411
which is part of Huayna Potosi,

00:18:47.932 --> 00:18:49.413
the highest peak in Bolivia.

00:18:50.354 --> 00:18:52.095
We have been studying this glacier since

00:18:55.057 --> 00:19:02.984
1991. There are small glaciers like Chacal Taya which are lower mountains.

00:19:03.324 --> 00:19:03.824
below

00:19:04.184 --> 00:19:04.784
5000 meters.

00:19:05.845 --> 00:19:08.546
This category of glaciers is destined to disappear.

00:19:10.346 --> 00:19:11.927
Only the highest glaciers,

00:19:11.987 --> 00:19:12.627
like the Zongo,

00:19:13.567 --> 00:19:16.008
El Huayna Potosi or Ilimani,

00:19:16.788 --> 00:19:19.269
will resist and not disappear completely.

00:19:19.789 --> 00:19:22.450
but will nevertheless suffer a significant setback.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:45.710
Once a month,

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:49.371
We are coming up here to measure the mass loss of the glacier.

00:19:50.752 --> 00:19:51.973
Over the last 30 years,

00:19:52.253 --> 00:19:55.174
The glaciers have retreated by 50 meters and that's far too much.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:01.381
The glacier is almost losing

00:20:02.462 --> 00:20:03.863
50 meters high.

00:20:03.883 --> 00:20:04.903
Oh yes ?

00:20:04.904 --> 00:20:05.344
Yes,

00:20:05.344 --> 00:20:07.245
That's a lot.

00:20:07.745 --> 00:20:08.766
And what is the cause?

00:20:09.606 --> 00:20:10.727
One of the main causes,

00:20:10.747 --> 00:20:11.968
It's climate change.

00:20:12.468 --> 00:20:14.169
But other factors come into play.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.291
With global warming,

00:20:16.932 --> 00:20:18.453
The melting is accelerating significantly.

00:20:19.554 --> 00:20:20.054
Look at,

00:20:20.234 --> 00:20:21.835
all the peaks you see over there in the distance,

00:20:21.855 --> 00:20:22.956
just a few years ago,

00:20:22.976 --> 00:20:24.337
They were snow-covered and now...

00:20:26.039 --> 00:20:26.500
And now,

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.360
There's nothing left.

00:20:28.541 --> 00:20:29.161
Effectively.

00:20:29.862 --> 00:20:32.464
The successive layers of ice have all disappeared.

00:20:38.268 --> 00:20:40.570
And there are also the fumes emitted by the factories,

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:41.290
gases.

00:20:41.531 --> 00:20:42.071
That must be a factor.

00:20:42.151 --> 00:20:42.651
No ?

00:20:45.469 --> 00:20:45.969
Yes,

00:20:47.751 --> 00:20:48.531
Without a doubt.

00:20:49.191 --> 00:20:53.354
This is a very serious problem because it's not just Bolivia that is affected.

00:20:53.914 --> 00:20:54.915
but the entire planet.

00:20:55.955 --> 00:20:57.896
Most of the energy we use,

00:20:58.477 --> 00:20:59.818
especially in developed countries,

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:00.838
fuels,

00:21:00.878 --> 00:21:01.378
gases,

00:21:02.219 --> 00:21:03.219
are harmful to the climate.

00:21:17.548 --> 00:21:19.215
Are there solutions to these problems?

00:21:24.664 --> 00:21:25.906
What are the solutions to prevent this?

00:21:25.926 --> 00:21:26.747
It's hard to say.

00:21:27.789 --> 00:21:28.289
Otherwise,

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:34.059
to consider obvious measures that would allow the planet to breathe and thus slow down climate change.

00:21:40.161 --> 00:21:42.482
This regression is not limited to Bolivia,

00:21:42.562 --> 00:21:44.002
but the entire Andes mountain range,

00:21:44.603 --> 00:21:46.103
and also the mountains of Europe,

00:21:46.403 --> 00:21:47.283
The Himalayas too.

00:21:48.384 --> 00:21:49.204
It's a global effect.

00:21:51.164 --> 00:21:51.485
NOW,

00:21:51.485 --> 00:21:57.466
We need to see how we adapt to this change and how people could consider common solutions.

00:22:00.607 --> 00:22:01.087
Obviously,

00:22:01.087 --> 00:22:03.968
These solutions should be considered at a local level.

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:08.563
But this is a problem we need to solve for all countries in the world.

00:22:23.133 --> 00:22:25.815
I am amazed.

00:22:25.875 --> 00:22:28.217
I never imagined I would one day be so close to heaven.

00:22:30.098 --> 00:22:31.139
I'm worried too.

00:22:33.152 --> 00:22:37.074
Edson and Patrick told me that we currently have more water than usual.

00:22:37.954 --> 00:22:40.536
but that a day will come when we will desperately lack it.

00:22:42.117 --> 00:22:46.639
How will our brothers and sisters and Mara manage to survive in this already very dry region?

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:49.100
It rains very little here.

00:22:50.161 --> 00:22:52.462
And I'm afraid they'll abandon their land because of it.

00:23:12.264 --> 00:23:15.306
Water from melting glaciers is abundant,

00:23:15.586 --> 00:23:16.406
but its management,

00:23:16.667 --> 00:23:19.988
Its distribution and the resources deployed are lacking.

00:23:20.329 --> 00:23:26.872
It was at the foot of the Tony Condoriri glacier that one of the two dams that supplies El Alto was built.

00:23:27.273 --> 00:23:30.314
It can collect up to 24 billion liters of water.

00:23:30.875 --> 00:23:35.277
In order to compensate for the retreat of glaciers and to meet the demand for water,

00:23:35.717 --> 00:23:40.320
Scientists agreed that new water reservoirs would be needed.

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:41.740
in the next five years.

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:43.221
But despite the urgency,

00:23:43.421 --> 00:23:45.241
Financial resources are lacking.

00:23:50.023 --> 00:23:53.063
The water from the glacier we visited is held back in this dam.

00:23:53.844 --> 00:23:56.264
We are taking advantage of the rain and the melting glacier.

00:23:57.145 --> 00:23:59.625
This water is stored and thus,

00:23:59.885 --> 00:24:00.966
during the dry season,

00:24:01.746 --> 00:24:02.566
We will not lack water.

00:24:04.147 --> 00:24:04.647
Of course.

00:24:09.928 --> 00:24:10.428
Ah,

00:24:10.428 --> 00:24:11.669
This is to avoid waste.

00:24:11.709 --> 00:24:12.209
Isn't that right?

00:24:13.330 --> 00:24:13.850
That's obvious.

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:16.331
So all of this comes from the glacier?

00:24:17.371 --> 00:24:17.871
Yes.

00:24:18.732 --> 00:24:23.054
The dam fills with rainwater and what comes from the melting glacier.

00:24:24.615 --> 00:24:25.095
The glacier,

00:24:25.095 --> 00:24:25.515
You see,

00:24:25.515 --> 00:24:26.876
functions like a dam.

00:24:27.216 --> 00:24:30.317
It retains the water in a snowy state and releases it little by little.

00:24:31.358 --> 00:24:33.118
They both function in a similar way.

00:24:44.385 --> 00:24:46.167
Could we also build dams elsewhere?

00:24:49.869 --> 00:24:50.370
Of course,

00:24:50.530 --> 00:24:51.190
That's desirable.

00:24:52.031 --> 00:24:52.871
And without a doubt,

00:24:52.872 --> 00:24:53.372
in the future,

00:24:53.812 --> 00:24:55.253
We will build several of them.

00:24:56.074 --> 00:24:58.255
in order to have water reserves in various places.

00:25:00.217 --> 00:25:04.520
But it is very difficult to find a suitable location for construction sites of this size.

00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:06.561
There are specialists,

00:25:06.641 --> 00:25:08.603
like hydroelectric engineers,

00:25:09.023 --> 00:25:10.164
who are thinking about this.

00:25:15.408 --> 00:25:17.190
And for cities as densely populated as Alto,

00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:18.431
That would be very desirable.

00:25:22.494 --> 00:25:22.995
Perfectly.

00:25:23.635 --> 00:25:24.135
And the Alto,

00:25:24.155 --> 00:25:24.816
as you know,

00:25:25.497 --> 00:25:26.858
is developing at a rapid pace.

00:25:27.999 --> 00:25:28.499
For now,

00:25:28.519 --> 00:25:30.501
We have some problems with the water.

00:25:30.981 --> 00:25:32.022
and in the years to come,

00:25:32.482 --> 00:25:33.503
They will intensify.

00:25:36.426 --> 00:25:38.347
Given climate change,

00:25:38.988 --> 00:25:40.309
The glaciers are receding,

00:25:40.890 --> 00:25:41.670
are shrinking.

00:25:43.212 --> 00:25:44.873
It is likely that in the coming years,

00:25:44.933 --> 00:25:47.195
We will have more water following the thaw.

00:25:48.016 --> 00:25:49.477
But this source will run out.

00:25:49.517 --> 00:25:51.719
then we will have to use rainwater.

00:25:53.801 --> 00:25:54.542
Although here too,

00:25:54.562 --> 00:25:55.663
There may be changes,

00:25:55.664 --> 00:25:57.244
It's possible that it will rain even less.

00:25:59.886 --> 00:26:01.468
And if the temperature rises even more,

00:26:02.128 --> 00:26:04.469
Some of the water retained here will evaporate.

00:26:05.930 --> 00:26:07.851
All of this will have serious consequences for us.

00:26:30.679 --> 00:26:32.000
Build another dam,

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:33.120
It's essential.

00:26:34.741 --> 00:26:37.381
But this will primarily benefit the city.

00:26:39.382 --> 00:26:43.563
Most people living in the vast countryside of the Altiplano do not have access to water.

00:26:44.463 --> 00:26:45.404
What will become of them?

00:26:55.552 --> 00:26:58.175
Oh,

00:26:58.176 --> 00:26:59.196
Ciao!

00:27:00.718 --> 00:27:01.158
Bye,

00:27:01.158 --> 00:27:01.658
Bye!

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:02.580
Hi,

00:27:08.647 --> 00:27:16.516
Wow!

00:27:22.828 --> 00:27:26.231
In order to better control water and its distribution in the Altiplano,

00:27:26.631 --> 00:27:28.473
We are building reservoirs.

00:27:28.753 --> 00:27:35.659
Most of them are supplied by water from dams and located halfway between the glacier and the villages.

00:27:35.999 --> 00:27:37.941
Kilometers of trenches are dug,

00:27:38.201 --> 00:27:42.625
Kilometers of pipes are laid to bring water to the communities.

00:27:43.025 --> 00:27:44.106
Only these tanks,

00:27:44.446 --> 00:27:47.529
smaller and significantly easier to build than dams,

00:27:47.889 --> 00:27:50.491
are still very rare in this desert region.

00:28:26.624 --> 00:28:28.365
Life is difficult in the altiplano.

00:28:29.665 --> 00:28:30.245
It's arid,

00:28:31.326 --> 00:28:31.946
it's cold,

00:28:33.267 --> 00:28:34.947
Few plants grow at this altitude.

00:28:37.128 --> 00:28:40.709
This is often not enough to support families who migrate to the city.

00:28:41.029 --> 00:28:42.290
thinking they would earn more money.

00:28:43.931 --> 00:28:44.731
Our cultures,

00:28:45.111 --> 00:28:47.152
Our traditions are declining with this exodus.

00:28:51.624 --> 00:28:55.646
I try, in my own small way, to keep the people I know in their village.

00:28:56.846 --> 00:28:59.447
Along with my other brothers and sisters who are members of the association,

00:29:00.048 --> 00:29:03.309
We are trying to develop the income of our communities in the Altiplano.

00:29:04.450 --> 00:29:09.972
We support them in their crafts which we collect and sell in fair trade shops in cities and in markets.

00:29:10.972 --> 00:29:13.454
We are also encouraging them to develop their agriculture.

00:29:13.694 --> 00:29:14.494
their craftsmanship,

00:29:14.974 --> 00:29:16.315
to educate the youngest children.

00:29:17.395 --> 00:29:18.996
I place a lot of emphasis on education.

00:29:21.408 --> 00:29:24.272
Each community receives my visit approximately once a month.

00:29:25.413 --> 00:29:25.913
Today,

00:29:26.415 --> 00:29:27.316
I'm going to Viliake.

00:29:27.836 --> 00:29:28.998
a rather poor village,

00:29:29.579 --> 00:29:32.683
which has very little water and does not yet have reservoirs.

00:29:34.185 --> 00:29:35.687
I plan to ask Doniato,

00:29:36.027 --> 00:29:37.769
one of the community leaders,

00:29:38.350 --> 00:29:39.632
if he has thought of any solutions.

00:29:40.152 --> 00:29:41.653
and what can be done.

00:29:49.238 --> 00:29:49.859
At Vilake,

00:29:50.679 --> 00:29:53.481
We have chosen the cooperative agricultural system.

00:29:55.022 --> 00:29:57.986
For the moment,
it is our village that is responsible for sowing the oats.

00:29:59.347 --> 00:30:00.328
In 4 or 5 years,

00:30:00.949 --> 00:30:02.711
The plan is to grow potatoes.

00:30:03.873 --> 00:30:05.915
But this culture is unpredictable.

00:30:05.935 --> 00:30:06.436
We need water.

00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:12.102
If we normally have rain,

00:30:13.203 --> 00:30:15.945
We harvest more or less enough for our subsistence.

00:30:17.486 --> 00:30:18.807
And if rain is scarce,

00:30:19.087 --> 00:30:19.928
We are experiencing a shortage.

00:30:23.491 --> 00:30:23.991
Look at,

00:30:23.991 --> 00:30:26.713
This oat crop did not grow as it should have due to the lack of rain.

00:30:28.995 --> 00:30:29.696
But last month,

00:30:29.697 --> 00:30:33.859
There was a big storm and the little fodder we had was damaged.

00:30:34.059 --> 00:30:34.840
As a result,

00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.862
It is our animals who suffer.

00:30:37.602 --> 00:30:38.643
SO...

00:30:39.804 --> 00:30:42.325
So there's no chance of seeing this oat grow any further?

00:30:43.185 --> 00:30:43.685
If,

00:30:43.806 --> 00:30:44.486
with God's help,

00:30:44.626 --> 00:30:46.347
we would like to implement irrigation,

00:30:46.747 --> 00:30:47.567
But it's not obvious.

00:30:48.588 --> 00:30:50.468
The terrain being uneven,

00:30:50.628 --> 00:30:54.450
This requires a lot of investment and at the moment we are blocked by a lack of resources.

00:30:58.432 --> 00:31:03.213
The best solution would be to bring water from the mountain via the Huayna Potosi glacier.

00:31:03.534 --> 00:31:06.375
who is up there.

00:31:15.004 --> 00:31:17.090
To solve this crucial irrigation problem,

00:31:17.330 --> 00:31:18.674
We would need to build a reservoir.

00:31:18.754 --> 00:31:19.254
No ?

00:31:19.596 --> 00:31:20.096
Quite.

00:31:20.316 --> 00:31:21.237
At the top of this hill,

00:31:21.257 --> 00:31:22.857
We could store water there.

00:31:23.477 --> 00:31:24.037
And what's more,

00:31:24.758 --> 00:31:26.718
It would blend in well with the landscape.

00:31:27.298 --> 00:31:28.339
It will be magnificent.

00:31:28.819 --> 00:31:31.460
We would use the rock to block the water.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:33.160
And by the grace of God,

00:31:33.660 --> 00:31:37.642
We would have a large water source that would supply the village,

00:31:38.002 --> 00:31:38.742
the inhabitants,

00:31:39.622 --> 00:31:40.322
animals,

00:31:40.823 --> 00:31:41.543
the crops.

00:31:41.863 --> 00:31:45.564
With its rugged terrain and hills covered in hard rock,

00:31:45.844 --> 00:31:48.605
That would be a difficult and formidable challenge.

00:31:48.985 --> 00:31:50.186
because it would be made by human hands.

00:31:50.566 --> 00:31:51.286
And is it urgent?

00:31:54.147 --> 00:31:55.248
The sooner the better.

00:31:56.288 --> 00:31:57.509
Can you describe the village to me?

00:31:58.409 --> 00:32:00.830
Villaque is made up of 6 zones,

00:32:01.170 --> 00:32:02.451
6 cantons if you prefer.

00:32:02.851 --> 00:32:04.372
And does everyone have the same need for water?

00:32:05.052 --> 00:32:05.612
Unfortunately,

00:32:05.792 --> 00:32:09.414
The repercussions on the population are being felt more and more each day.

00:32:10.014 --> 00:32:10.594
Currently,

00:32:11.014 --> 00:32:12.635
There are still 700 families,

00:32:12.895 --> 00:32:13.755
But for how long?

00:32:14.616 --> 00:32:15.436
We see it every day.

00:32:15.536 --> 00:32:22.327
Leaving for El Alto, the village is becoming depopulated, the hemorrhage must be stopped, so you can understand the urgent need for work and that it is crucial for those who remain.

00:32:22.327 --> 00:32:33.888
This particularly affects young people, who are the most impacted, and some who migrate to the city in search of work because here, once the planting season is over, the countryside is deserted.

00:32:33.888 --> 00:32:37.035
There's nothing to be done here, the ground is too dry

00:32:39.633 --> 00:32:40.093
SO,

00:32:40.093 --> 00:32:41.494
with good investments,

00:32:41.694 --> 00:32:44.435
It would be possible for us to cultivate everything that can be found in the region.

00:32:45.196 --> 00:32:49.378
We could even expand the arable areas with the virgin land that is up there.

00:32:50.618 --> 00:32:52.740
What is the land area surrounding the village?

00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:54.801
Just around Villake,

00:32:55.441 --> 00:32:57.662
We have 15,300 hectares.

00:33:00.384 --> 00:33:02.205
Do you realize if all of this has been cultivated?

00:33:02.565 --> 00:33:03.065
Yes,

00:33:03.465 --> 00:33:04.566
That's a lot of land.

00:33:04.586 --> 00:33:05.507
but to work with them,

00:33:05.867 --> 00:33:08.128
We would need to bring back those who have left.

00:33:09.189 --> 00:33:09.929
Another great challenge.

00:33:15.033 --> 00:33:16.674
With easier access to water,

00:33:17.174 --> 00:33:21.057
Many villages in the Altiplano could grow any vegetables they wanted.

00:33:21.617 --> 00:33:22.898
to provide for their needs,

00:33:23.358 --> 00:33:26.681
to become self-sufficient and thus put a stop to rural exodus,

00:33:27.001 --> 00:33:31.684
which is a source of suffering for the Emara people, who are so attached to their land and traditions.

00:33:38.924 --> 00:33:44.230
The old sorcerer Pedro invokes Pachamama for good rains during the next harvest.

00:33:45.331 --> 00:33:48.794
He also asks her to help the community with the construction of a reservoir.

00:35:11.436 --> 00:35:12.657
Today I am happy.

00:35:13.337 --> 00:35:17.259
I will be attending the launch of the construction of a drinking water reservoir in Palcoco.

00:35:17.699 --> 00:35:18.640
a village on the Plateau.

00:35:20.201 --> 00:35:25.343
I will be able to find out more and pass the solution on to Doniato and the other ICAB communities.

00:35:27.104 --> 00:35:28.825
All beneficiaries of the reservoir,

00:35:29.125 --> 00:35:31.286
those from Palcoco, but also from neighboring villages

00:35:31.786 --> 00:35:34.768
are gathering today to begin the community project.

00:35:36.244 --> 00:35:38.465
Whenever major works are undertaken,

00:35:39.165 --> 00:35:41.266
We ask for protection from Pachamama.

00:35:42.267 --> 00:35:43.468
It's a tradition in our family.

00:35:43.948 --> 00:35:44.748
and a real party.

00:35:48.950 --> 00:35:50.151
To achieve their goal,

00:35:50.471 --> 00:35:55.693
The villagers and municipal authorities must show patience and determination.

00:35:56.494 --> 00:35:56.994
Often,

00:35:57.334 --> 00:36:01.076
Several years of negotiations are needed to convince the communities.

00:36:01.484 --> 00:36:06.027
Obtain the necessary administrative authorizations and finally begin the work.

00:36:06.527 --> 00:36:09.529
All that's needed is to capture the springs flowing down from the glacier.

00:36:10.210 --> 00:36:11.591
Once the process is initiated,

00:36:12.071 --> 00:36:17.895
A few weeks are enough to dig kilometers of trenches that connect the reservoir and the homes.

00:36:17.896 --> 00:36:19.436
The vital existence of nature is one of the first things that allows us to do.

00:36:19.436 --> 00:36:26.481
The total number of these reservoirs is firmly in the minds of the families who will benefit from this providential water.

00:36:29.263 --> 00:36:30.424
My dearest brothers,

00:36:30.444 --> 00:36:31.685
my dearest sisters,

00:36:31.805 --> 00:36:33.286
gentlemen specialists.

00:36:34.527 --> 00:36:38.170
Today we are here to keep you informed about the Colonna project,

00:36:39.071 --> 00:36:40.212
which must start right now.

00:36:41.585 --> 00:36:44.647
We are going to begin work on the drinking water reservoir.

00:36:45.268 --> 00:36:46.869
planned within the framework of this project,

00:36:46.949 --> 00:36:48.450
while respecting our traditions.

00:36:49.931 --> 00:36:52.673
Among us are the leaders of Viluyo,

00:36:53.014 --> 00:36:53.894
Machacamarca,

00:36:54.695 --> 00:36:55.235
Palcoco,

00:36:55.676 --> 00:36:56.296
Condoriri,

00:36:56.476 --> 00:36:57.117
Coastline,

00:36:57.177 --> 00:36:57.917
Villa Andino.

00:36:59.118 --> 00:37:01.540
We are all committed to successfully completing this project.

00:37:03.041 --> 00:37:06.104
The division of tasks will be explained to you before the start of the work.

00:37:07.041 --> 00:37:10.508
Let us not forget to respect our rituals of offerings to the earth and sea.

00:37:11.410 --> 00:37:12.292
Pachamama,

00:37:12.733 --> 00:37:13.935
to the forces of the mountain.

00:37:14.677 --> 00:37:15.519
Thank you for listening to me.

00:37:15.599 --> 00:37:16.160
dear brothers,

00:37:16.281 --> 00:37:16.782
Dear sisters.

00:37:31.415 --> 00:37:32.016
Dear brothers,

00:37:32.096 --> 00:37:32.876
Dear sisters,

00:37:32.976 --> 00:37:34.897
We will now give the floor to Gerarda.

00:37:35.637 --> 00:37:38.778
which represents the Association of Producers and Artisans of Bolivia.

00:37:39.198 --> 00:37:39.659
It's your turn.

00:37:39.659 --> 00:37:40.159
Gerarda.

00:37:45.061 --> 00:37:45.561
THANKS,

00:37:45.581 --> 00:37:46.141
dear brothers,

00:37:46.241 --> 00:37:46.782
Dear sisters.

00:37:48.042 --> 00:37:50.343
Hello to the representatives of the Palcoco town hall,

00:37:51.043 --> 00:37:52.764
to the eight representatives of the communities.

00:37:53.724 --> 00:37:58.887
"I am very happy to be among you this morning and delighted that this project is finally coming to fruition.

00:37:59.787 --> 00:38:01.868
This is a great day for everyone here.

00:38:10.071 --> 00:38:10.812
“Last Saturday,

00:38:10.852 --> 00:38:19.135
I went up onto the glacier with glaciologists and they explained to me the evolution of the climate and water in relation to global warming.

00:38:22.817 --> 00:38:28.861
I am pleased to know that you are going to build a water reservoir and that you will be able to lay the first stone today.

00:38:30.081 --> 00:38:33.363
The glaciologists told me that in a few years we are going to run out of water.

00:38:33.883 --> 00:38:35.604
We must therefore be careful.

00:38:37.125 --> 00:38:39.727
I was able to witness the phenomenon with my own eyes.

00:38:44.229 --> 00:38:48.972
This water reservoir is essential and many more will need to be built in the coming years.

00:41:07.112 --> 00:41:09.793
At the beginning of this project, which dates back to 2003,

00:41:10.413 --> 00:41:11.814
We were only two communities.

00:41:13.414 --> 00:41:15.895
Then all the other communities joined us.

00:41:17.475 --> 00:41:19.436
They understood that living with other communities,

00:41:19.436 --> 00:41:20.656
with the same comfort as in the city,

00:41:21.056 --> 00:41:22.157
was a good motivation.

00:41:22.957 --> 00:41:25.598
And then we started talking about the melting glaciers,

00:41:25.958 --> 00:41:26.918
And that was decisive.

00:41:30.959 --> 00:41:33.920
The sole purpose of this work is access to drinking water.

00:41:34.180 --> 00:41:35.680
essential for everyone's survival.

00:41:40.502 --> 00:41:42.342
All of this has taken on considerable proportions.

00:41:43.522 --> 00:41:44.763
I remain convinced that,

00:41:45.083 --> 00:41:45.823
with God's help,

00:41:46.203 --> 00:41:47.163
and thanks to our faith,

00:41:47.804 --> 00:41:48.544
We will succeed.

00:41:52.747 --> 00:41:58.211
Today, with this inaugural first stone, we are reaching the point where the irrigation system can be extended.

00:42:04.716 --> 00:42:11.242
Will all communities benefit from this project?

00:42:11.702 --> 00:42:13.904
This is for the seven communities,

00:42:14.044 --> 00:42:16.026
My brother.

00:42:16.027 --> 00:42:16.906
And from there onward,

00:42:17.747 --> 00:42:18.708
It will be useful.

00:42:19.488 --> 00:42:20.349
All communities,

00:42:20.369 --> 00:42:20.869
obviously.

00:42:21.710 --> 00:42:26.693
The architect who designed the drinking water reservoir made sure that everyone could benefit from this water.

00:42:27.174 --> 00:42:28.014
I am very confident.

00:42:28.915 --> 00:42:32.397
Our goal will be achieved through the solidarity of each and every one of us.

00:42:51.780 --> 00:42:56.623
Despite this natural spirit of solidarity among the Indians and Maras of the Altiplano,

00:42:57.143 --> 00:42:59.505
Reservoir projects are still too rare.

00:42:59.605 --> 00:43:06.208
due to a lack of initiative and especially because of often precarious technical and financial resources.

00:45:03.577 --> 00:45:08.361
The majority of the fragmented land belongs to communities that must pay for access to water.

00:45:08.362 --> 00:45:11.004
Some private landowners have made an effort to ensure that the fragmented land can be reused.

00:45:11.104 --> 00:45:13.005
have the means to have private access

00:45:13.085 --> 00:45:18.249
which allows them to practice irrigation on the altiplano for extensive crops.

00:45:18.849 --> 00:45:20.991
They also develop specific techniques,

00:45:21.311 --> 00:45:22.692
such as drip irrigation,

00:45:23.012 --> 00:45:26.254
which requires very little water while ensuring good yields.

00:45:26.795 --> 00:45:29.857
Faced with global warming and water scarcity,

00:45:30.237 --> 00:45:33.980
It's a method that allows you to use less water and use it better.

00:45:34.500 --> 00:45:38.002
This drip irrigation technique pays for itself in one year.

00:45:38.423 --> 00:45:39.643
With two harvests per year,

00:45:39.644 --> 00:45:40.204
It allows...

00:45:40.444 --> 00:45:44.107
to a farmer to live better than an employee in the city of El Alto.

00:45:50.212 --> 00:45:51.373
I'm going to Calamarca.

00:45:52.114 --> 00:45:53.895
I am going to meet Walter Fernandez.

00:45:54.116 --> 00:45:54.956
a farmer,

00:45:55.457 --> 00:45:57.699
who will show me this drip irrigation technique.

00:45:59.040 --> 00:46:02.903
I am curious to see with my own eyes what he manages to do in the altiplano.

00:46:07.006 --> 00:46:08.468
As you have seen,

00:46:09.176 --> 00:46:09.697
Everything is dry.

00:46:10.459 --> 00:46:13.424
It is winter and almost the entire harvest has been completed.

00:46:13.945 --> 00:46:14.567
as you can see.

00:46:23.797 --> 00:46:25.778
And when was the irrigation stopped?

00:46:26.678 --> 00:46:27.678
It's been two weeks.

00:46:28.418 --> 00:46:28.918
Normally,

00:46:28.999 --> 00:46:30.639
We should have stopped more than a month ago.

00:46:33.220 --> 00:46:34.500
Is that why it's drying out like that?

00:46:35.180 --> 00:46:35.680
Yes,

00:46:36.100 --> 00:46:37.261
but thanks to this method,

00:46:37.481 --> 00:46:39.081
We had a very good first harvest.

00:46:41.262 --> 00:46:44.803
But irrigating the fields only affects part of our production.

00:46:47.203 --> 00:46:49.104
Here,
the drip method is used.

00:46:49.824 --> 00:46:50.825
in the greenhouses at the back.

00:46:52.166 --> 00:46:52.666
Besides,

00:46:52.866 --> 00:46:54.568
all our remaining harvests are there.

00:46:56.209 --> 00:46:56.709
Right now,

00:46:56.749 --> 00:46:58.330
We produce potatoes there.

00:47:08.057 --> 00:47:08.797
Potatoes.

00:47:09.298 --> 00:47:09.858
And what else?

00:47:10.659 --> 00:47:11.359
Beans,

00:47:11.780 --> 00:47:12.360
onions,

00:47:12.420 --> 00:47:13.361
sometimes carrots

00:47:14.421 --> 00:47:15.042
peas,

00:47:15.062 --> 00:47:15.682
salads,

00:47:17.043 --> 00:47:17.924
but also barley.

00:47:18.288 --> 00:47:19.228
to feed the livestock.

00:47:24.670 --> 00:47:26.251
How many harvests do you have in a year?

00:47:27.511 --> 00:47:31.073
We start sowing in August and we harvest twice a year.

00:47:33.834 --> 00:47:36.014
And all of this is possible thanks to irrigation?

00:47:36.815 --> 00:47:37.315
Yes,

00:47:37.615 --> 00:47:40.656
Water is needed constantly and the land must be worked continuously.

00:47:42.284 --> 00:47:43.905
Is it useful to other communities?

00:47:45.705 --> 00:47:46.205
No,

00:47:46.205 --> 00:47:47.706
We are a private organization.

00:47:48.306 --> 00:47:51.287
We are not associated with the other farmers.

00:47:55.148 --> 00:47:56.928
And where does your irrigation water come from?

00:48:00.409 --> 00:48:03.570
We pay for our access to the community drinking water source.

00:48:05.831 --> 00:48:09.612
But since this water must be distributed equally among everyone,

00:48:10.136 --> 00:48:15.020
We also invested in a personal water pump that draws its water from a lower source.

00:48:17.162 --> 00:48:19.504
This water is used for the fields.

00:48:19.664 --> 00:48:20.765
whereas for the greenhouse,

00:48:21.285 --> 00:48:23.747
we only use the one from the community.

00:48:25.209 --> 00:48:25.709
Of course,

00:48:25.729 --> 00:48:29.232
If there is a restriction or if we have an additional need,

00:48:29.852 --> 00:48:32.455
We cannot take drinking water from the community.

00:48:36.238 --> 00:48:36.898
So in that case,

00:48:36.938 --> 00:48:38.299
Are you using your water pump?

00:48:38.440 --> 00:48:38.940
Yes.

00:48:39.160 --> 00:48:41.541
Otherwise,
we risk a confrontation with the community.

00:48:42.042 --> 00:48:43.182
And that would be a problem for us.

00:48:54.008 --> 00:48:56.109
And is there always water in the surrounding area?

00:48:56.410 --> 00:48:56.910
Yes,

00:48:56.930 --> 00:48:57.390
here,

00:48:57.390 --> 00:48:57.950
There is water,

00:48:58.591 --> 00:48:59.931
but it is very poorly distributed.

00:49:00.012 --> 00:49:00.812
That's the only problem.

00:49:01.772 --> 00:49:02.272
SO,

00:49:02.273 --> 00:49:04.354
we should only use it for domestic purposes.

00:49:05.615 --> 00:49:07.916
We must never forget that in other places,

00:49:08.312 --> 00:49:13.274
There is no water at all.

00:49:25.539 --> 00:49:27.420
I've never seen so many vegetables in my life.

00:49:27.780 --> 00:49:28.541
That's incredible.

00:49:29.461 --> 00:49:30.501
Each backblow produced.

00:49:31.962 --> 00:49:32.802
That amazed me.

00:49:33.883 --> 00:49:36.424
I can't wait to tell my brothers and sisters all about this.

00:49:37.324 --> 00:49:42.868
Having such greenhouses would change their lives and would stop the depopulation of villages once and for all.

00:49:50.453 --> 00:49:52.134
Whether it's dams,

00:49:52.274 --> 00:49:54.096
reservoirs or drip irrigation,

00:49:54.316 --> 00:49:56.818
Solutions exist for future water shortages.

00:49:58.179 --> 00:49:58.679
Only,

00:49:58.979 --> 00:50:04.483
They must be put in place very quickly and on a large scale to retain this water that is rushing down the mountains.

00:50:05.063 --> 00:50:05.924
But how do we do it?

00:50:06.104 --> 00:50:08.526
when you are one of the poorest countries on the planet,

00:50:08.946 --> 00:50:13.089
endowed with a GDP of only $2.60 per capita,

00:50:13.389 --> 00:50:18.413
and that we are suffering the climatic consequences of a development from which we have never benefited.

00:50:19.053 --> 00:50:19.694
Waiting for,

00:50:20.214 --> 00:50:24.077
Glaciers are melting and 2 million people depend on them today.

00:50:26.299 --> 00:50:28.801
I don't know what will happen in 10 or 20 years.

00:50:29.441 --> 00:50:32.323
Will our communities in the Altiplano have enough greenhouses?

00:50:32.483 --> 00:50:33.284
of tanks?

00:50:33.524 --> 00:50:34.484
to stay up there,

00:50:34.524 --> 00:50:36.065
As close as possible to the gods in Tchatchilas?

00:50:36.765 --> 00:50:38.726
We all have a part of the answer.

00:50:39.306 --> 00:50:40.007
For my part,

00:50:40.587 --> 00:50:42.948
I will continue my travels across the Altiplano,

00:50:43.548 --> 00:50:45.409
to support my brothers and sisters and my rat,

00:50:46.049 --> 00:50:47.690
so that our traditions may live on.

00:50:47.930 --> 00:50:50.311
our culture and our small villages.

00:50:50.991 --> 00:50:51.671
But in the future,

00:50:51.771 --> 00:50:53.232
I'm going to tell them what I saw.

00:50:54.032 --> 00:50:56.513
It is possible to fight against the lack of water.

00:50:57.174 --> 00:50:59.495
It is our turn to watch over Pachamama,

00:50:59.835 --> 00:51:00.495
land-sea,

00:51:01.135 --> 00:51:01.775
so that once again,

00:51:02.376 --> 00:51:03.096
She watches over us.

